WEBVTT

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.580
Before you start a run,

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.240
make five quick checks.

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:05.470
First, are you signed into

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:06.770
the right AutoLander account

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:08.190
with access to the work

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:09.210
you're about to do?

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.760
Second, is Facebook connected?

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:13.310
Check the indicator

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:14.330
at the top right.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.300
If it needs attention, go

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.430
to Configuration, then Facebook,

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:20.060
and follow the connection steps.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.120
Third, is the inventory right?

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.900
Open Post to Market

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.040
and look for a few

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.220
vehicles you recognize

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.700
from the correct dealership.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.740
If you're

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:30.960
setting up your own feed,

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.120
the inventory lesson

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:33.500
shows the connection steps.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.260
If your dealership

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.460
already manages it,

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.040
use that existing feed.

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:39.990
Fourth, is

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.510
the vehicle ready to advertise?

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:43.950
Check its price and mileage,

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.990
your selection count, and any

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.670
optional AI credit cost.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.360
Resolve incorrect

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:51.320
information before posting it.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.040
Fifth, is the computer online

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.500
with AutoLander running?

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:58.190
If you use Auto-Pilot, check

00:00:58.190 --> 00:00:59.570
that it's on and configured

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:00.810
for the window you want.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.740
Now read any

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:03.880
unfinished Queue item

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.340
before starting another job.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:06.660
If something

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:07.700
still doesn't match,

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.280
you've narrowed down the issue.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.560
Dealer-account users can

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:12.820
take that specific problem

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.640
to their manager; individual

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.900
users can contact the AutoLander

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.100
admin through Support.

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:20.340
Pause and do those five

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.700
checks on your own screen.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.360
Write down only

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.740
the item that needs attention.
